+# Ralue Editor open-source release obligations
+
+Ralue Editor is a modified distribution of Collabora Online source covered
+primarily by the Mozilla Public License 2.0 (MPL-2.0). This file is an
+engineering release checklist, not legal advice.
+
+Before a public binary or hosted client bundle is released:
+
+1. Publish the corresponding Ralue Editor source revision, including every
+   modified MPL-covered file, under MPL-2.0.
+2. Keep `COPYING`, `README.FILENOTICES.md`, per-file SPDX notices, copyright
+   notices, source history, and the third-party notices in `browser/LICENSE`.
+3. Put a durable source-code link on the download/release page and on the
+   public open-source notice page. The link must identify the exact source tag
+   matching the distributed image and browser revision.
+4. Do not use Collabora names, logos, product marks, or domains as Ralue's
+   product identity. Historical attribution and license notices must remain.
+5. Publish image provenance: upstream engine digest, Ralue image digest,
+   source tag, browser revision, license identifier, and build instructions.
+6. Run the trademark scan and a clean source build before release; review any
+   remaining runtime-facing Collabora marks. Source comments, history, and
+   factual attribution are not product branding and must not be stripped.
+7. Keep the proprietary Career Hub application separate from the MPL source
+   release. New files that contain no MPL-covered code are not automatically
+   required to use MPL merely because they communicate with Ralue Editor.
+
+The release is not compliant merely because the repository exists: the source
+link must be available to recipients of the matching executable/client bundle.
+
+Authoritative references:
+
+- https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/
+- https://www.mozilla.org/MPL/2.0/FAQ/
+- https://www.collaboraonline.com/trademark-policy/
